    "lists": {
      "ordered": [
        {
          "text": "**Atomicity:** An atomic note contains a single, discrete idea or concept.",
          "indent_level": 0,
          "line_number": 69,
          "source": "pkb-report-core-principles-creating-durable-and-discoverable-knowledge-assets-20251120092640.md"
        },
        {
          "text": "**Clarity:** The note must be written *for your future self*, who has forgotten the original context. This means writing in complete sentences, defining jargon, and fully articulating the idea.",
          "indent_level": 0,
          "line_number": 71,
          "source": "pkb-report-core-principles-creating-durable-and-discoverable-knowledge-assets-20251120092640.md"
        },
        {
          "text": "**Connections (Links):** The explicit, usually bidirectional, links *between* notes. This is the digital equivalent of Luhmann's associative trails. A note's true power is not what it *contains*, but what it *connects to*.",
          "indent_level": 0,
          "line_number": 81,
          "source": "pkb-report-core-principles-creating-durable-and-discoverable-knowledge-assets-20251120092640.md"
        },
        {
          "text": "**Provenance:** The implicit context of a note's origin. *Why* did I write this? *What* was the source? *When* did I write it? This information provides the backstory that your future self will need to re-establish the note's relevance.",
          "indent_level": 0,
          "line_number": 83,
          "source": "pkb-report-core-principles-creating-durable-and-discoverable-knowledge-assets-20251120092640.md"
        },
        {
          "text": "**It Externalizes Cognition:** This system becomes a trusted \"second brain.\" By offloading the *storage* and *connection* of ideas to a durable, discoverable system, you free your biological brain to do what it does best: *think*, *create*, and *synthesize*.",
          "indent_level": 0,
          "line_number": 163,
          "source": "pkb-report-core-principles-creating-durable-and-discoverable-knowledge-assets-20251120092640.md"
        },
        {
          "text": "**It Combats Context Collapse:** We are flooded with context-free information (like a tweet). This method forces you to re-establish context, embedding each new piece of information into your existing web of knowledge.",
          "indent_level": 0,
          "line_number": 165,
          "source": "pkb-report-core-principles-creating-durable-and-discoverable-knowledge-assets-20251120092640.md"
        },
        {
          "text": "**It Creates an Intellectual Flywheel:** The more assets you create using this system, the more valuable the *entire system* becomes. The linking possibilities (Context) grow exponentially, leading to more novel connections and insights.",
          "indent_level": 0,
          "line_number": 166,
          "source": "pkb-report-core-principles-creating-durable-and-discoverable-knowledge-assets-20251120092640.md"
        },
        {
          "text": "Can I find a note in my current system from 3+ years ago and *immediately* understand its full meaning and source? If not, which of the three pillars (Content, Context, Metadata) failed?",
          "indent_level": 0,
          "line_number": 197,
          "source": "pkb-report-core-principles-creating-durable-and-discoverable-knowledge-assets-20251120092640.md"
        },
        {
          "text": "What is the \"atomicity\" of a note, and why is it a prerequisite for building rich Context?",
          "indent_level": 0,
          "line_number": 199,
          "source": "pkb-report-core-principles-creating-durable-and-discoverable-knowledge-assets-20251120092640.md"
        },
        {
          "text": "Explain the difference between \"Metadata\" and \"Context.\" How can a link be considered both?",
          "indent_level": 0,
          "line_number": 200,
          "source": "pkb-report-core-principles-creating-durable-and-discoverable-knowledge-assets-20251120092640.md"
        },
        {
          "text": "What is the \"symbiotic loop\"? How does creating good Content make it easier to create good Metadata and Context?",
          "indent_level": 0,
          "line_number": 201,
          "source": "pkb-report-core-principles-creating-durable-and-discoverable-knowledge-assets-20251120092640.md"
        },
        {
          "text": "What is the primary counter-argument against this system, and what is the response to that critique?",
          "indent_level": 0,
          "line_number": 202,
          "source": "pkb-report-core-principles-creating-durable-and-discoverable-knowledge-assets-20251120092640.md"
        },
        {
          "text": "Ahrens, S. (2017). *How to Take Smart Notes: One Simple Technique to Boost Writing, Learning and Thinking*. CreateSpace Independent Publishing Platform.",
          "indent_level": 0,
          "line_number": 205,
          "source": "pkb-report-core-principles-creating-durable-and-discoverable-knowledge-assets-20251120092640.md"
        },
        {
          "text": "Bush, V. (1945, July). As We May Think. *The Atlantic Monthly*.",
          "indent_level": 0,
          "line_number": 207,
          "source": "pkb-report-core-principles-creating-durable-and-discoverable-knowledge-assets-20251120092640.md"
        },
        {
          "text": "Luhmann, N. (1992). Communicating with Slip Boxes: An Empirical Account. In A. Kieserling (Ed.), *Universität also Milieu*. Haux.",
          "indent_level": 0,
          "line_number": 208,
          "source": "pkb-report-core-principles-creating-durable-and-discoverable-knowledge-assets-20251120092640.md"
        },
        {
          "text": "Matuschak, A. (2019). *Evergreen notes*. Retrieved from [https://notes.andymatuschak.org/Evergreen_notes](https://notes.andymatuschak.org/Evergreen_notes).",
          "indent_level": 0,
          "line_number": 209,
          "source": "pkb-report-core-principles-creating-durable-and-discoverable-knowledge-assets-20251120092640.md"
        },
        {
          "text": "Tiago Forte (2022). *Building a Second Brain: A Proven Method to Organize Your Digital Life and Unlock Your Creative Potential*. Atria Books.",
          "indent_level": 0,
          "line_number": 210,
          "source": "pkb-report-core-principles-creating-durable-and-discoverable-knowledge-assets-20251120092640.md"
        }
      ],
      "unordered": [
        {
          "text": "**Library Science:** For centuries, librarians have wrestled with discoverability. Systems like the Dewey Decimal Classification or the Library of Congress system are massive metadata frameworks designed to make a physical piece of content (a book) discoverable. They standardized metadata (author, subject, publication date) to solve this problem.",
          "indent_level": 0,
          "line_number": 53,
          "source": "pkb-report-core-principles-creating-durable-and-discoverable-knowledge-assets-20251120092640.md"
        },
        {
          "text": "**Vannevar Bush (1945):** In his seminal essay \"As We May Think,\" Bush conceptualized the \"Memex.\" He envisioned a machine that would store all a person's books, records, and communications, but its true power was its ability to create associative trails—**links**—between them. This was the conceptual birth of context-driven knowledge.",
          "indent_level": 0,
          "line_number": 55,
          "source": "pkb-report-core-principles-creating-durable-and-discoverable-knowledge-assets-20251120092640.md"
        },
        {
          "text": "**Niklas Luhmann (Zettelkasten):** The most potent practical example comes from German sociologist Niklas Luhmann. He built a \"slip-box\" (Zettelkasten) of over 90,000 *paper* notes. His legendary productivity (over 70 books and 400 articles) was not due to his memory, but his system.",
          "indent_level": 0,
          "line_number": 56,
          "source": "pkb-report-core-principles-creating-durable-and-discoverable-knowledge-assets-20251120092640.md"
        },
        {
          "text": "**Content:** Each note was **atomic**, containing one idea.",
          "indent_level": 2,
          "line_number": 57,
          "source": "pkb-report-core-principles-creating-durable-and-discoverable-knowledge-assets-20251120092640.md"
        },
        {
          "text": "**Metadata:** Each note had a unique ID (e.g., 21/3d7a).",
          "indent_level": 2,
          "line_number": 58,
          "source": "pkb-report-core-principles-creating-durable-and-discoverable-knowledge-assets-20251120092640.md"
        },
        {
          "text": "**Context:** This ID system was not hierarchical; it was *associative*. A note on one topic could be physically placed to branch off another, and explicit links (references to other note IDs) were added. Luhmann \"conversed\" with his slip-box, following these trails of context.",
          "indent_level": 2,
          "line_number": 59,
          "source": "pkb-report-core-principles-creating-durable-and-discoverable-knowledge-assets-20251120092640.md"
        },
        {
          "text": "**Digital Gardening & Evergreen Notes:** Modern concepts like \"Digital Gardens\" (championed by Andy Matuschak) translate Luhmann's ideas to the digital realm. The focus is on creating **\"Evergreen Notes\"**—assets that are written to evolve, connect, and last a lifetime.",
          "indent_level": 0,
          "line_number": 60,
          "source": "pkb-report-core-principles-creating-durable-and-discoverable-knowledge-assets-20251120092640.md"
        },
        {
          "text": "`title:` A clear, descriptive title.",
          "indent_level": 0,
          "line_number": 96,
          "source": "pkb-report-core-principles-creating-durable-and-discoverable-knowledge-assets-20251120092640.md"
        },
        {
          "text": "`aliases:` Other names you might use to search for this (e.g., \"Second Brain\" for a note on \"Zettelkasten\").",
          "indent_level": 0,
          "line_number": 98,
          "source": "pkb-report-core-principles-creating-durable-and-discoverable-knowledge-assets-20251120092640.md"
        },
        {
          "text": "`tags:` Broad categories (e.g., `#philosophy`, `#physics`).",
          "indent_level": 0,
          "line_number": 99,
          "source": "pkb-report-core-principles-creating-durable-and-discoverable-knowledge-assets-20251120092640.md"
        },
        {
          "text": "`status:` A workflow state (e.g., `[🌱seed]`, `[🌳evergreen]`).",
          "indent_level": 0,
          "line_number": 100,
          "source": "pkb-report-core-principles-creating-durable-and-discoverable-knowledge-assets-20251120092640.md"
        },
        {
          "text": "`source:` The bibliographic citation or URL.",
          "indent_level": 0,
          "line_number": 101,
          "source": "pkb-report-core-principles-creating-durable-and-discoverable-knowledge-assets-20251120092640.md"
        },
        {
          "text": "Atomic **Content** is *easier* to link, which creates rich **Context**.",
          "indent_level": 0,
          "line_number": 106,
          "source": "pkb-report-core-principles-creating-durable-and-discoverable-knowledge-assets-20251120092640.md"
        },
        {
          "text": "This rich **Context** (a web of links) *is itself* a powerful form of metadata, allowing you to discover related ideas by traversal, not just by search.",
          "indent_level": 0,
          "line_number": 108,
          "source": "pkb-report-core-principles-creating-durable-and-discoverable-knowledge-assets-20251120092640.md"
        },
        {
          "text": "Structured **Metadata** (like a `tag`) allows you to query your system to find a *cluster* of notes, revealing emergent **Contexts** (patterns) you didn't know existed.",
          "indent_level": 0,
          "line_number": 109,
          "source": "pkb-report-core-principles-creating-durable-and-discoverable-knowledge-assets-20251120092640.md"
        },
        {
          "text": "A note with clear **Content** but no **Context** (links) or **Metadata** (tags) is an orphan—durable, but undiscoverable.",
          "indent_level": 0,
          "line_number": 110,
          "source": "pkb-report-core-principles-creating-durable-and-discoverable-knowledge-assets-20251120092640.md"
        },
        {
          "text": "A note with great **Metadata** and **Context** but cryptic **Content** is a dead-end—discoverable, but not durable.",
          "indent_level": 0,
          "line_number": 111,
          "source": "pkb-report-core-principles-creating-durable-and-discoverable-knowledge-assets-20251120092640.md"
        },
        {
          "text": "**Atomic Titles:** The title is your first piece of metadata. It should be a clear assertion or a precise description (e.g., \"Light Follows Geodesics in Curved Spacetime\").",
          "indent_level": 0,
          "line_number": 118,
          "source": "pkb-report-core-principles-creating-durable-and-discoverable-knowledge-assets-20251120092640.md"
        },
        {
          "text": "**Elaborate in Your Own Words:** This forces synthesis, which is the first step to durability. A copy-pasted quote is not a knowledge asset; it's a warehouse.",
          "indent_level": 0,
          "line_number": 120,
          "source": "pkb-report-core-principles-creating-durable-and-discoverable-knowledge-assets-20251120092640.md"
        },
        {
          "text": "**Define Jargon:** Assume your future self is a smart-but-forgetful stranger.",
          "indent_level": 0,
          "line_number": 121,
          "source": "pkb-report-core-principles-creating-durable-and-discoverable-knowledge-assets-20251120092640.md"
        },
        {
          "text": "**Explicit Linking:** As you write, actively ask: \"What does this relate to?\" and create explicit `[[bidirectional links]]` to those other notes.",
          "indent_level": 0,
          "line_number": 124,
          "source": "pkb-report-core-principles-creating-durable-and-discoverable-knowledge-assets-20251120092640.md"
        },
        {
          "text": "**Implicit Context:** Use a `source:` field in your metadata to capture provenance. A quick \"Why I wrote this:\" note can also be invaluable.",
          "indent_level": 0,
          "line_number": 126,
          "source": "pkb-report-core-principles-creating-durable-and-discoverable-knowledge-assets-20251120092640.md"
        },
        {
          "text": "**Failure Mode (The \"Digital Attic\"):**",
          "indent_level": 0,
          "line_number": 146,
          "source": "pkb-report-core-principles-creating-durable-and-discoverable-knowledge-assets-20251120092640.md"
        },
        {
          "text": "**System:** A single \"notes.txt\" file or a dump of Word documents.",
          "indent_level": 2,
          "line_number": 148,
          "source": "pkb-report-core-principles-creating-durable-and-discoverable-knowledge-assets-20251120092640.md"
        },
        {
          "text": "**Content:** Cryptic, non-atomic (a \"kitchen sink\" file).",
          "indent_level": 2,
          "line_number": 149,
          "source": "pkb-report-core-principles-creating-durable-and-discoverable-knowledge-assets-20251120092640.md"
        },
        {
          "text": "**Context:** Non-existent. No links.",
          "indent_level": 2,
          "line_number": 150,
          "source": "pkb-report-core-principles-creating-durable-and-discoverable-knowledge-assets-20251120092640.md"
        },
        {
          "text": "**Metadata:** Non-existent, save for the OS file date.",
          "indent_level": 2,
          "line_number": 151,
          "source": "pkb-report-core-principles-creating-durable-and-discoverable-knowledge-assets-20251120092640.md"
        },
        {
          "text": "**Result:** Total knowledge loss. The system is undiscoverable and non-durable.",
          "indent_level": 2,
          "line_number": 152,
          "source": "pkb-report-core-principles-creating-durable-and-discoverable-knowledge-assets-20251120092640.md"
        },
        {
          "text": "**Success Mode (The \"Digital Garden\"):**",
          "indent_level": 0,
          "line_number": 153,
          "source": "pkb-report-core-principles-creating-durable-and-discoverable-knowledge-assets-20251120092640.md"
        },
        {
          "text": "**System:** A linked-note-based system (e.g., Obsidian, Zettelkasten).",
          "indent_level": 2,
          "line_number": 154,
          "source": "pkb-report-core-principles-creating-durable-and-discoverable-knowledge-assets-20251120092640.md"
        },
        {
          "text": "**Content:** Atomic, clearly written notes.",
          "indent_level": 2,
          "line_number": 155,
          "source": "pkb-report-core-principles-creating-durable-and-discoverable-knowledge-assets-20251120092640.md"
        },
        {
          "text": "**Context:** A dense web of links between notes.",
          "indent_level": 2,
          "line_number": 156,
          "source": "pkb-report-core-principles-creating-durable-and-discoverable-knowledge-assets-20251120092640.md"
        },
        {
          "text": "**Metadata:** Rich YAML front-matter (tags, aliases, sources).",
          "indent_level": 2,
          "line_number": 157,
          "source": "pkb-report-core-principles-creating-durable-and-discoverable-knowledge-assets-20251120092640.md"
        },
        {
          "text": "**Result:** A generative system. A search for `tag: #thermodynamics` (Metadata) surfaces 15 notes (Content), and exploring their links (Context) allows you to synthesize a new argument for an essay. The system *itself* generates new insights.",
          "indent_level": 2,
          "line_number": 158,
          "source": "pkb-report-core-principles-creating-durable-and-discoverable-knowledge-assets-20251120092640.md"
        },
        {
          "text": "**The Tooling Problem:** Do our current tools create \"lock-in\"? Is a proprietary metadata or linking format (like Roam Research's) a risk to long-term durability? This has fueled the rise of plain-text systems like Obsidian.",
          "indent_level": 0,
          "line_number": 178,
          "source": "pkb-report-core-principles-creating-durable-and-discoverable-knowledge-assets-20251120092640.md"
        },
        {
          "text": "**The AI Revolution:** How will generative AI and large-language models (LLMs) impact this?",
          "indent_level": 0,
          "line_number": 180,
          "source": "pkb-report-core-principles-creating-durable-and-discoverable-knowledge-assets-20251120092640.md"
        },
        {
          "text": "Will AI be able to *generate* the context and metadata for our messy, unstructured notes, making this human-led effort obsolete?",
          "indent_level": 2,
          "line_number": 181,
          "source": "pkb-report-core-principles-creating-durable-and-discoverable-knowledge-assets-20251120092640.md"
        },
        {
          "text": "Or, will a well-structured personal knowledge graph (built on this triad) become the *ultimate* fine-tuning dataset to create a personalized AI assistant that truly \"thinks\" like you?",
          "indent_level": 2,
          "line_number": 182,
          "source": "pkb-report-core-principles-creating-durable-and-discoverable-knowledge-assets-20251120092640.md"
        },
        {
          "text": "**The Friction Problem:** This system requires deliberate, upfront effort. This \"activation energy\" is a significant barrier.",
          "indent_level": 0,
          "line_number": 183,
          "source": "pkb-report-core-principles-creating-durable-and-discoverable-knowledge-assets-20251120092640.md"
        }
      ]
    },
